.TH OMX-COMPLEMENT-SYNC 1 "2026-10-28" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-complement-sync \- give the inferred port groups to every LV2 plugin that lacks them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-complement-sync
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --verbose ]
.br
.B omx-complement-sync
.B --check
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each installed LV2 bundle on the LV2 search list holding a plugin whose port groups
.B omx-panel complement
infers with confidence, writes a bundle named omx-complement-<bundle>.lv2 in MODGUI_DIR. It restates every TTL file lilv reads for the installed bundle, statement for statement, keeps lv2:binary pointing at the installed library, raises each plugin's lv2:microVersion by one (lv2:minorVersion unchanged), and adds the group nodes (lv2:symbol, lv2:name, lv2:displayPriority) and pg:group on each grouped port. lilv then loads it in place of the installed bundle. Every other file of the installed bundle is linked in, so a plugin that reads its own files finds them.
.PP
The installed bundle is never touched. Deleting the written bundle is the whole removal: lilv loads the installed one again.
.PP
Nothing is written for a bundle none of whose plugins needs groups: a plugin that carries its own, fits one screen of four, or has no confident grouping is left exactly as it is.
.PP
A bundle whose marker file .omx-complement-sync names the same installed bundle, the same content hash and the same writer is left as it is. A bundle of that name without the marker is never written. A marked bundle no longer wanted is named as stale and left in place.
.PP
A bundle the restatement cannot carry is refused, named with its reason, and never fails the run: TTL the reader cannot parse, a version that is not an integer or is at lilv's ceiling, more than one version or binary for a plugin, a plugin declared in more than one installed bundle, a dynamic manifest, a data file outside the bundle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
say what would be written, and change nothing
.TP
.B --verbose
also print each plugin's verdict: grouped (with its groups), nothing to do or no confident grouping (with the reason)
.TP
.B --check
change nothing and report: the LV2 search list and where it came from, whether MODGUI_DIR is on it, and whether the LV2_PATH that the mod-host and mod-ui units run with holds MODGUI_DIR
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LV2_PATH
the LV2 search list. Unset, it is plugin-hostd's default: /usr/lib64/lv2:/usr/lib/lv2:/usr/local/lib/lv2
.TP
.B MODGUI_DIR
the bundles, omx-modgui-sync's directory (default /usr/local/lib/lv2 for root, ~/.lv2 for a user). It must be on the LV2_PATH the plugin hosts read
.TP
.B STATE_DIR
the work files, omx-modgui-sync's (default /var/lib/omx/modgui-sync; $XDG_DATA_HOME/omx/modgui-sync for a user other than root)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/omx/modgui-sync.conf
KEY=value lines for the variables above, read by the unit, shared with omx-modgui-sync
.TP
.I omx-complement-sync.service
runs the sync once; installed but not enabled (systemctl enable omx-complement-sync). Enabled, it runs at boot and each time plugin-qualify-sync finishes (a drop-in, plugin-qualify-sync.service.d/omx-complement-sync.conf, queues it from ExecStartPost when the unit is enabled).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the run finished, whatever it refused; or --check reported
.TP
.B 1
the run could not start
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-modgui-sync (1),
.BR omx-panel (1)
